      "registry-driver-profile": {
        "ClusterId": "registry-svc",
        "Order": 10,
        "AuthorizationPolicy": "anonymous",
        "Match": { "Path": "/v1/drivers/profile" },
        "Metadata": { "RateLimit": "write" }
      },

      "registry-driver-profile-photo": {
        "ClusterId": "registry-svc",
        "Order": 10,
        "AuthorizationPolicy": "anonymous",
        "//": [
          "Δ MCS-25. The bytes behind the avatar both driver apps draw. `anonymous` here is the",
          "same posture every other signed-link read on this table has: the caller is an image",
          "loader and carries no bearer token, so registry-svc's HMAC is the credential and the",
          "gateway has nothing to check that the service does not check better.",
          "",
          "`default` rather than `write` — it is a GET, and it is fetched once per screen open."
        ],
        "Match": { "Path": "/v1/drivers/{driverId}/profile-photo" },
        "Metadata": { "RateLimit": "default" }
      },

      "registry-driver-payout-profile": {
        "ClusterId": "registry-svc",
        "Order": 10,
        "AuthorizationPolicy": "anonymous",
        "//": [
          "AL-58's payout plane (C133), added in C124's CI repair. payout.yaml and registry.yaml",
          "declared seven public operations when payout-svc landed in wave 3 and the gateway was",
          "never given the cluster: four were unrouted 404s and three fell through to admin-bff,",
          "which does not serve them. The gateway is the only way a driver or an admin reaches",
          "them, so payout-svc was deployed and unreachable — RouteTableTests had been red on main",
          "since 2026-08-01 saying exactly that.",
          "",
          "The profile lives on registry-svc (its contract is registry.yaml) while the payouts",
          "themselves live on payout-svc. Two services under one /v1/drivers/payout* prefix, which",
          "is why these are literal Order-10 routes rather than one wildcard."
        ],
        "Match": { "Path": "/v1/drivers/payout-profile" },
        "Metadata": { "RateLimit": "write" }
      },
      "registry-driver-payout-documents": {
        "ClusterId": "registry-svc",
        "Order": 10,
        "AuthorizationPolicy": "anonymous",
        "//": [
          "Its own route rather than payout-profile/{**remainder}, so a future sub-resource is not",
          "swallowed without anybody choosing to.",
          "",
          "'write', not an upload-specific policy: Gateway.RateLimits.Policies defines admin, auth,",
          "default, geo, public-track, realtime, sos and write, and every other document upload in",
          "this table uses write. A dedicated upload bucket may be worth having — a multipart POST",
          "is not the same load as a JSON PUT — but inventing a policy inside a routing fix is how",
          "a rate limit ends up with no thought behind it."
        ],
        "Match": { "Path": "/v1/drivers/payout-profile/documents" },
        "Metadata": { "RateLimit": "write" }
      },
      "payout-driver-payouts": {
        "ClusterId": "payout-svc",
        "Order": 10,
