      "iam-jwks": {
        "ClusterId": "iam-svc",
        "Order": 50,
        "AuthorizationPolicy": "anonymous",
        "Match": { "Path": "/v1/.well-known/jwks.json" },
        "//": [
          "Δ C126. The public half of the RS256 signing key (D-29, D-21), which EVERY service fetches",
          "to validate a bearer — and which nothing could reach before this route existed.",
          "",
          "In the Kubernetes layout each service is a pod and `http://iam-svc/.well-known/jwks.json`",
          "resolves. In BOTH compose stacks iam-svc is one of 22 services co-located inside",
          "app-services and CoLocatedHost binds it on 127.0.0.1, so the only cross-container HTTP",
          "surface that container has is this gateway. env/.env.common.example asked for",
          "`/v1/internal/iam/.well-known/jwks.json`, which is refused ahead of routing by",
          "BlockedPathMiddleware and was never a route here: every JWT-validating service therefore",
          "answered 500 to every authenticated request, in dev as much as on the replica. Nothing had",
          "noticed because the fetch happens on the first request that carries a token, not at",
          "readiness — and the smoke suite asserts 401s, which need no key.",
          "",
          "PATH REWRITE, and the /v1 prefix is why: RouteConfigurationTests holds the edge to",
          "/v1, /public and /hubs, while the endpoint iam-svc actually serves (and that the JWKS",
          "specification expects) is at the root. The gateway is the right place for that difference.",
          "",
          "VersionGate exempt: a service fetching a key sends none of D-31's client headers, and a 426",
          "here would break authentication platform-wide rather than ask anybody to upgrade."
        ],
        "Metadata": {
          "RateLimit": "default",
          "VersionGate": "exempt"
        },
        "Transforms": [ { "PathSet": "/.well-known/jwks.json" } ]
      },
